{"title":"2024 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Simple_and_easy_to_make_sense_of)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Simple and easy to make sense of)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_(Goes_through_full_thought_process)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle (Goes through full thought process)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve_(crystal_clear)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve (crystal clear)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn.org\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn.org</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_NiuniuMaths_(Easy_to_understand!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by NiuniuMaths (Easy to understand!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">22</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A group of frogs (called an army) is living in a tree. A frog turns green when in the shade and turns yellow\nwhen in the sun. Initially, the ratio of green to yellow frogs was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98bd0f90c5e7da2f5a58b36fabf8761b52f1f3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 : 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> green frogs moved to the\nsunny side and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yellow frogs moved to the shady side. Now the ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df8ce1b5ddb31e060e4d25e61661b6c94764e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 : 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. What is the difference\nbetween the number of green frogs and the number of yellow frogs now? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17a3cd1697471fe100a33afa809ad137452c8a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 10\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 12\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 16\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 20\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the initial number of green frogs be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and the initial number of yellow frogs be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Since the ratio of the number of green frogs to yellow frogs is initially <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98bd0f90c5e7da2f5a58b36fabf8761b52f1f3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 : 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f1863383171e5cd8dd216b3afc9e804b39ee76f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = 3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> green frogs move to the sunny side and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yellow frogs move to the shade side, thus the new number of green frogs is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dc1725d12c987392e56201ea792052a14bb5df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> and the new number of yellow frogs is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/f/22f19b415f313b60ecaabac3e4a0d26d496c9f14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />. We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad1d1fa269c2acc705fe9cb910270bc6508443c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{g + 2}{y - 2} = \\frac{4}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"84\" height=\"42\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/59423076a71c9362b8fc00c5ab5baad335909d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g + 2 = 4y - 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f1863383171e5cd8dd216b3afc9e804b39ee76f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = 3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/332161cedb4a5700a6e08556e202ecb851d88bd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y + 2 = 4y - 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c4d4d271c5c4dc51fcf7c5e2dee14a7c7fae47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b1dc17bd07e19b1397e55d878a5e16cf0075ca0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e9fbfc782f292808aece3099cb3a137ef047f14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(g + 2) - (y - 2) = 32 - 8 = \\boxed{(E) \\hspace{1 mm} 24}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"300\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>-anonchalantdreadhead\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the original ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b610da333cd721fae3e3346701af4a1cf7481b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" /> and the new ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff3c81ca2426fed69bc7607dde1f79286c1b855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, the number of frogs must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the only solutions left are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/313048c3149436615f6cd06b7f1bec83420d6a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/a/02ad991c2821130f0d7e456d453252c19a320752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(E)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />.  \n</p><p>Let's start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> frogs: \n</p><p>We must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> frogs in the shade and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> frogs in the sun. After the change, there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> frogs in the shade and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> frog in the sun, which is not a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff3c81ca2426fed69bc7607dde1f79286c1b855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" /> ratio. \n</p><p>Therefore the answer is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5d8bef0cb175b6abf21f6d248a0acf3dbfc1ff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(E) \\hspace{1 mm} 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>-ILoveMath31415926535\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Simple_and_easy_to_make_sense_of.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Simple_and_easy_to_make_sense_of)\">Solution 3 (Simple and easy to make sense of)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Simple and easy to make sense of)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (green) to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (yellow) frogs is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b610da333cd721fae3e3346701af4a1cf7481b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> green frogs move to the sunny side and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yellow frogs move to the shady side, the ratio becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8c877d8f2922008ffb30f1905bbde56ef59774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g + 2:y - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff3c81ca2426fed69bc7607dde1f79286c1b855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>So earlier, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4dfc7d496ed3365432fba7268cdb962064b894b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, of the total frogs were green. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fd03d5b164ae8b40db27a6f8ddb20d9d43f95fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/f/40f3a94845aa68a9f536c5075ba8752e3e3fa37b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, of the total frogs are green. When the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> frogs transferred from the yellow side to the green, the green side gained <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/1/1e19c4697dd55656f6c93e36ec31050657a592d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> of the total amount of frogs. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/1/1e19c4697dd55656f6c93e36ec31050657a592d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the total number of frogs. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84fe2c6c764983c11d2e1b34521316d434a9536b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4: 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> has a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then we can multiply each of them by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/a/9ba3fe23e79115ff883c84f3c83505e44f3ac2ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{40}{(4 + 1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"60\" height=\"43\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and find that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> green frogs and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yellow frogs. Therefore, the difference between the green and yellow frogs is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/235f421dc86a068b66ffe480464e7c50f301ce24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~mihikamishra\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/OwJvuq6F7sQ\">https://youtu.be/OwJvuq6F7sQ</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/29xcfUcmTgg\">https://youtu.be/29xcfUcmTgg</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/BaE00H2SHQM?si=yTyYiS2S75HoSfmI&amp;t=6313\">https://youtu.be/BaE00H2SHQM?si=yTyYiS2S75HoSfmI&amp;t=6313</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_.28Goes_through_full_thought_process.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_(Goes_through_full_thought_process)\">Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle (Goes through full thought process)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsect